{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:25:30.743Z","ordinal":16362,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b02e-7a81-7bf1-8757-64a5247d115a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac147724fc87d08f701247fcd67c29","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Done:\n\n- Ignored `.playwright-mcp/`.\n- Deleted untracked `err.log` (it was an old cargo-audit yanked-`bisync` diagnostic).\n- Committed the relevant Markdown and action change as `37e1ac6 docs(agents): enforce sibling-gap discipline`.\n\nThe action change is important: it defaults release PR versioning to `callisto version --refresh-lockfiles`, preventing the lockfile-drift failure. I also shortened its description.\n\nThe Entire-search files came from a prior Entire managed setup on September 11: the same generated skill was installed across `.agents`, `.claude`, `.codex`, `.gemini`, and `.opencode`, all with the same timestamp and `ENTIRE-MANAGED SEARCH SKILL` marker. They predate this release-recovery work. The available history confirms prior Entire setup/hardening work but does not identify the exact creating command. I left those untracked and untouched."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789662327162,"completed_at_ms":1789662330743}}
